      "path": "/guides/handle-scope-creep/",
      "title": "How to Handle Scope Creep on Fixed-Fee Projects | ScopeLedger",
      "titleLength": 61,
      "description": "A practical process for fixed-fee agencies: compare requests with agreed scope, estimate costs, choose a response and confirm the next step in writing.",
      "descriptionLength": 151,
      "headings": [
        {
          "level": "h1",
          "text": "Handle scope creep before the next small yes."
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Check what changed in the agreement."
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Estimate the work before you answer."
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "text": "A small request with a measurable cost"
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Choose an explicit response."
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Give the client a calm, specific next step."
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "text": "For an additional fee"
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "text": "For an exchange"
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "text": "For a later phase"
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Put the decision and approval in writing."
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Try the workflow with the sample project."
        },
        {
          "level": "h2",
          "text": "Related guides"
        }
